## 2. Color System

### 2.1 Color Palette Strategy
- [ ] **Single brand color + neutrals** (Stripe, Linear style)
- [ ] **Extended palette** — Primary, secondary, accent, semantic (success/warning/error)
- [ ] **Data visualization palette** — Categorical, sequential, diverging scales
- [ ] **Custom per-customer theming** (Enterprise white-label)

### 2.2 Base Palette Definition
| Token | Light Value | Dark Value | Usage |
|-------|-------------|------------|-------|
| `color-brand-50` | `#eff6ff` | `#1e3a5f` | Lightest brand tint |
| `color-brand-100` | `#dbeafe` | `#1e426e` | ... |
| `color-brand-500` | `#3b82f6` | `#60a5fa` | **Primary brand** |
| `color-brand-600` | `#2563eb` | `#3b82f6` | Hover/active |
| `color-neutral-50` | `#fafafa` | `#0a0a0a` | Background base |
| `color-neutral-900` | `#171717` | `#fafafa` | Text primary |
| `color-success-500` | `#22c55e` | `#4ade80` | Success states |
| `color-warning-500` | `#f59e0b` | `#fbbf24` | Warning states |
| `color-error-500` | `#ef4444` | `#f87171` | Error states |

> **Note**: Use 50-950 scale (Tailwind convention). Define all 11 steps per hue.

